# Keeps the Docker build context small and keeps host state out of the image.
# PR-18 owns the multi-stage image: it installs and builds INSIDE the image, so the compiled
# apps/server/dist and apps/web/dist are produced there rather than copied from a developer machine.
# `**/dist` is therefore ignored — a release must not be shippable from a build that happened to be lying
# around in someone's checkout, and `tsc` does not delete output whose source has gone away. The Dockerfile
# deletes the three dists again before building, so the guarantee survives anyone editing this file.
#
# **Every pattern below is anchored at the context root**, because that is how Docker matches them: unlike
# .gitignore, a `.dockerignore` entry applies only where it is written, so plain `node_modules` matches the
# root's and NOT `apps/server/node_modules` — which is where a workspace install actually puts everything, and
# `COPY . .` would pour it over the tree the image had just installed (CI cannot see this class of mistake,
# because its runner has run `pnpm install` in the same checkout seconds earlier). Hence the `**/` prefixes on
# the three host-build artefacts: they are the ones a developer's tree has at every level.
.git
.github
.clinerules
docs

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.pnpm-store

# A real .env must never reach an image; the template is documentation, not runtime input.
.env
.env.*

coverage
coverage-unit
coverage-integration
playwright-report
test-results

# Browser tests run on the host/CI, never inside the image (PR-19).
apps/web/e2e

.dev
*.log
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode
